    "result_text": "The full test suite is green: **264 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ownerSegment` field \u2014 a read-time derived value formatted `<TIER>_<AREA>` \u2014 following the existing pattern for derived owner fields (`locality`, `timezone`, `ageBand`, etc.).\n\n**Two changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `ownerSegment` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(target = \"ownerSegment\", expression = \"java(ownerSegment(owner))\")` and the corresponding default method:\n   - **TIER** = `PREMIUM` when `membershipLevel >= 3`, else `STANDARD` (null level \u2192 `STANDARD`).\n   - **AREA** = `METRO` when the owner's derived `locality(owner)` is a known region (NSW/VIC/QLD \u2014 checked via the existing `REGION_TIMEZONE` table, which is keyed exactly on those three), else `REGIONAL`.\n\nThis reuses the mapper's existing `locality(owner)` derivation, so `ownerSegment` stays consistent with the already-published `locality`/`timezone` fields. The two new acceptance tests (`STANDARD_METRO` for Sydney/NSW, `STANDARD_REGIONAL` for an unknown city) pass, and no existing test regressed.",
